  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS SIDS Fiji 2025 &#x2013; Desk Study 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fiji, one of the world&#x2019;s most climate-vulnerable nations, faces growing risks from floods and cyclones, resulting in an estimated annual loss of 500 million FJD (approx. 230 million USD). The Ba region, in particular, is highly affected by recurring river flooding caused by climate change, intense rainfall, and deforestation. These floods lead to significant economic disruption, with short-term solutions like river dredging often having negative environmental impacts. The objective of this Dutch Disaster Risk Reduction and Surge Support (DRRS) scoping assignment is to assess the current situation and to identify any gaps in urgent technical support needed.</narrative>
  </description>
